<Section collapsed="false" isCollapsible="true" drawButton="true" MultipleChoiceAnswerIndex="-1" MultipleChoiceRandomizeChoices="false" TrueFalseAnswerIndex="-1" EssayAnswerRows="5" EssayAnswerColumns="60"><Title><Text-field style="Heading 1" layout="Heading 1">WS6 -- Example 8: Euler equations, rotation symmetry (p = 0)</Text-field></Title>
<Section collapsed="false" isCollapsible="true" drawButton="true" MultipleChoiceAnswerIndex="-1" MultipleChoiceRandomizeChoices="false" TrueFalseAnswerIndex="-1" EssayAnswerRows="5" EssayAnswerColumns="60"><Title><Text-field style="Heading 2" layout="Heading 2">Setup</Text-field></Title>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L2" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">restart;
# WS6: verification of Example 8, Section 8.6 (incompressible 2D Euler equations,
# rotation symmetry, energy conservation law, p = 0; Section 7, Remark 12).
# u1 = u, u2 = v, u3 = P; omega_hat as in eq. (7.2).
# All CHECKs must print 0 (3 checkpoints).
with(DifferentialGeometry): with(JetCalculus):
K := 4:
DGsetup([t, x, y], [u1, u2, u3], J, K):
Vol := evalDG(Dt &amp;wedge Dx &amp;wedge Dy):
F1 := u1[1] + u1[]*u1[2] + u2[]*u1[3] + u3[2]:
F2 := u2[1] + u1[]*u2[2] + u2[]*u2[3] + u3[3]:
F3 := u1[2] + u2[3]:
Kd := (u1[]^2 + u2[]^2)/2:
omega_hat := evalDG( Kd * Dx &amp;wedge Dy
   - u1[]*(Kd + u3[]) * Dt &amp;wedge Dy
   + u2[]*(Kd + u3[]) * Dt &amp;wedge Dx ):</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
</Section>
<Section collapsed="false" isCollapsible="true" drawButton="true" MultipleChoiceAnswerIndex="-1" MultipleChoiceRandomizeChoices="false" TrueFalseAnswerIndex="-1" EssayAnswerRows="5" EssayAnswerColumns="60"><Title><Text-field style="Heading 2" layout="Heading 2">The energy conservation law</Text-field></Title>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L3" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal"># CHECK 1 (expect 0): the multiplier identity (8.4), d_0(omega_hat) = (u F1 + v F2 + (K+P) F3) dt^dx^dy.
evalDG( HorizontalExteriorDerivative(omega_hat)
   - (u1[]*F1 + u2[]*F2 + (Kd + u3[])*F3) * Vol );</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
</Section>
<Section collapsed="false" isCollapsible="true" drawButton="true" MultipleChoiceAnswerIndex="-1" MultipleChoiceRandomizeChoices="false" TrueFalseAnswerIndex="-1" EssayAnswerRows="5" EssayAnswerColumns="60"><Title><Text-field style="Heading 2" layout="Heading 2">Rotation invariance</Text-field></Title>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L4" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal"># Rotation generator Y = x d_y - y d_x + u d_v - v d_u + 0 d_P (prolonged to the jet space).
Ypt := evalDG( x*D_y - y*D_x + u1[]*D_u2[] - u2[]*D_u1[] ):
PY  := Prolong(Ypt, K):
# CHECK 2 (expect 0): L_Y omega_hat = 0 (hence also condition (7.1), L_Y d_0 omega_hat = 0).
evalDG( LieDerivative(PY, omega_hat) );</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
</Section>
<Section collapsed="false" isCollapsible="true" drawButton="true" MultipleChoiceAnswerIndex="-1" MultipleChoiceRandomizeChoices="false" TrueFalseAnswerIndex="-1" EssayAnswerRows="5" EssayAnswerColumns="60"><Title><Text-field style="Heading 2" layout="Heading 2">The reduction: -Y _| omega_hat</Text-field></Title>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L5" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal"></Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L9" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="J &gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal"># CHECK 3 (expect 0): the reduction -Y _| omega_hat (Section 7, vartheta_hat = 0) equals
# K (x dx + y dy) - (xu + yv)(K + P) dt, Example 8; in polar coordinates K r dr - w (K + P) dt.
# Hook does not accept vector fields with horizontal components on biforms
# (Dx, Dy, Dt are dual to total derivatives), so the contraction is done with
# omega_hat converted to an ordinary differential form on the jet space.
</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L11" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="J &gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">omega_form := convert(omega_hat, DGform);
</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L13" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="J &gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">red    := evalDG( -Hook(PY, omega_form) );
</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L15" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
